# Build context for the Go backend image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` into the build stage. Without this file the
# daemon receives the whole repository — 292 MB, of which 280 MB is
# web/node_modules that the Go build has no use for. That made a cold backend
# build take minutes of pure context transfer.
#
# This is also the standing guard against baking a credential into a build
# layer: anything matched here cannot reach the image even if someone later
# leaves a secret in the working tree.

# The frontend. Codex builds and ships it separately; the API image contains
# only Go binaries.
web/

# VCS and CI metadata.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Secrets and local environment. .env.example is a committed template with no
# real values, but excluding the whole family is the safer default — an
# allowlist for one file is not worth the risk of the next .env being missed.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
*credentials*

# Test, coverage and profiling output.
tests/load/results/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.test
*.prof
*.pprof

# Documentation and design records. They belong in the repository, not in a
# runtime image.
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Local tooling and editor state.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
.claude/
bin/
tmp/
